  "description": "Erection of single storey ground floor side infill extension",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its poor design, size, massing, and location, would result in an obtrusive and incompatible form of development that fails to be subservient to the original dwelling house and fails to respect the architectural integrity of the subject property, the terrace of which it forms part, and the wider area. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) and D4 (Delivering good design) of The London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).",
    "The proposal,&amp;nbsp; by reason of its size, height, and depth on the boundary, would result in a harmful impact on the amenities of the neighbouring occupiers at No. 15 Denver Road by way of a loss of light and outlook, and would have an overbearing and tunnelling impact. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D6 (Housing quality and standards) of the London Plan (2021), policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).&amp;nbsp;"
  ],
